Treeker is updated to version 1.2, with the following changes:

- The game now has a dialog box on launch. You can configure Screen Resolution, V-sync On and Off quality options, and change Key Inputs;

- The game is now compatible and configured for Xbox 360 controller. The game may accept other controller options as well, but it's not guaranteed. It's recommended activating V-Sync if you have high framerate, to prevent the camera from having unexpected behavior when using a controller;

- Invert Camera Y-Axis and option to disable Motion Blur are now available on Settings option in-game, which can be accessed from main menu;

- The puzzle of the transparent bridge in the last island has been remade. Previously players could solve the puzzle unexpectedly due to a code failure, even without understanding entirely the puzzle;

- New content coming soon to Treeker. Treeker: Shard of the Lens will be a new game mode, free of charge for all Treeker: The Lost Glasses players. Now when you complete the game, this mode will be unlocked, and will be available to play immediately when it's released. More details soon.

Notice that currently, controllers will only work on gameplay, and not on menus. Also, the interface in-game will show default key inputs.

Thanks for the feedback.

